    "notes": "Craig Stobo is a highly experienced NZ professional director with a distinguished career spanning diplomacy, economics, investment banking and fund management. Key roles include CEO of BT Funds Management (1992-2004), Chair of FMA (2024-2026, resigned after neutrality investigation), Chair of Precinct Properties, LGFA, AIG NZ, and Elevation Capital. Authored the 2004 taxation report that led to the PIE regime. Resigned as FMA Chair in May 2026 following Wendy Aldred KC investigation finding political neutrality breaches.",
